    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "can u explain how a standard 3-step progressive discipline policy usually works? i just started as a manager and want to make sure i handle things right if someone is underperforming",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A standard 3-step progressive discipline policy provides a clear, escalating path for addressing employee performance or conduct issues. Typically, it starts with a verbal warning, followed by a written warning if the behavior continues. The third step is usually a final written warning, which may lead to further action like suspension or termination if the issue persists. This structure ensures employees are aware of expectations and given opportunities for improvement before severe consequences occur.",
